IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc10-libel.l4 -- sections 297 to 317 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: defamatory libel (the definition of newspaper, defamatory libel and
-- publishing; the offences; the cases in which a person is not deemed to publish; the verdict). Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (every element holds, or the immunity applies); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words, quoted in the branch's comment);
-- NOTHING (not covered: an element is missing, the text is silent or limits a prohibition in its own wording, or the answer points outside the text).
-- A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Seams: `s 297 ...` is answered here for ccc15 (s 478(5)); `s 787(1) ...` is ccc29's. The text says "he" throughout ss 303 to 316
-- (and "them" in ss 298 and 300): the functions say "the person".

§ `s 297 -- Definition of newspaper`

-- 297: "newspaper means": a closed definition, so JUST FALSE outside it. Two limbs. Intervals are the longest interval in days between two issues.
-- src:5913 | 297 In sections 303, 304 and 308, newspaper means any paper, magazine or periodical containing public news, intelligence or reports of events, or any remarks or observations thereon, printed for sale and published periodically or in parts or numbers, at intervals not exceeding thirty-one days between the publication of any two such papers, parts or numbers, and any paper, magazine or periodical printed in order to be dispersed and made public, weekly or more often, or at intervals not exceeding thirty-one days, that contains advertisements, exclusively or principally.
@ref s 297 (src:5913)
GIVEN `the publication is a paper, magazine or periodical` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains public news, intelligence or reports of events, or any remarks or observations thereon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is printed for sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published periodically or in parts or numbers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longest interval in days between the publication of any two such papers, parts or numbers` IS A NUMBER
      `it is printed in order to be dispersed and made public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it contains advertisements, exclusively or principally` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 297 the publication is a newspaper` MEANS
    IF    (`the publication is a paper, magazine or periodical` AND `it contains public news, intelligence or reports of events, or any remarks or observations thereon` AND `it is printed for sale` AND `it is published periodically or in parts or numbers` AND `the longest interval in days between the publication of any two such papers, parts or numbers` AT MOST 31)
       OR (`the publication is a paper, magazine or periodical` AND `it is printed in order to be dispersed and made public` AND `the longest interval in days between the publication of any two such papers, parts or numbers` AT MOST 31 AND `it contains advertisements, exclusively or principally`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "newspaper means any paper, magazine or periodical" (a "means" definition: the publication is within neither limb)

@ref s 297 (src:5913)
GIVEN section IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 297 the definition applies in the section` MEANS
    IF section's `section` EQUALS 303 OR section's `section` EQUALS 304 OR section's `section` EQUALS 308
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In sections 303, 304 and 308, newspaper means"

§ `ss 298 and 299 -- Defamatory libel and publishing`

-- 298(1): "A defamatory libel is matter published, without lawful justification or excuse, that ...": a definition by "is", read as closed (fork F45).
-- src:5914 | Definition
-- src:5915 | 298 (1) A defamatory libel is matter published, without lawful justification or excuse, that is likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing him to hatred, contempt or ridicule, or that is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published.
@ref s 298(1) (src:5914-5915)
GIVEN `the matter is published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is lawful justification or excuse for publishing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing him to hatred, contempt or ridicule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 298(1) the matter is a defamatory libel` MEANS
    IF `the matter is published` AND (NOT `there is lawful justification or excuse for publishing it`) AND (`it is likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing him to hatred, contempt or ridicule` OR `it is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A defamatory libel is matter published, without lawful justification or excuse, that is likely to injure the reputation of any person by exposing him to hatred, contempt or ridicule, or that is designed to insult the person of or concerning whom it is published" (a definition by "is", read as closed: F45)

DECLARE `s 298(2) the manner of expression` IS ONE OF
    `s 298(2) directly`
    `s 298(2) by insinuation`
    `s 298(2) by irony`
    `s 298(2) in another manner`

DECLARE `s 298(2) the medium` IS ONE OF
    `s 298(2)(a) in words legibly marked on any substance`
    `s 298(2)(b) by any object signifying a defamatory libel otherwise than by words`
    `s 298(2) in another medium`

-- src:5916 | Mode of expression
-- src:5917 | (2) A defamatory libel may be expressed directly or by insinuation or irony
-- src:5918 | (a) in words legibly marked on any substance; or
-- src:5919 | (b) by any object signifying a defamatory libel otherwise than by words.
@ref s 298(2) (src:5916-5919)
GIVEN manner IS A `s 298(2) the manner of expression`
      medium IS A `s 298(2) the medium`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 298(2) a defamatory libel may be expressed in this manner and medium` MEANS
    IF manner EQUALS `s 298(2) in another manner` OR medium EQUALS `s 298(2) in another medium`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be expressed directly or by insinuation or irony" and "(a) in words legibly marked on any substance; or (b) by any object" say what may be, and do not close the list
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5921 | 299 A person publishes a libel when he
-- src:5922 | (a) exhibits it in public;
-- src:5923 | (b) causes it to be read or seen; or
-- src:5924 | (c) shows or delivers it, or causes it to be shown or delivered, with intent that it should be read or seen by any person other than the person whom it defames.
@ref s 299 (src:5921-5924)
GIVEN `the person exhibits it in public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person causes it to be read or seen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person shows or delivers it, or causes it to be shown or delivered, with intent that it should be read or seen by any person other than the person whom it defames` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 299 the person publishes a libel` MEANS
    IF `the person exhibits it in public` OR `the person causes it to be read or seen` OR `the person shows or delivers it, or causes it to be shown or delivered, with intent that it should be read or seen by any person other than the person whom it defames`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person publishes a libel when he" (none of (a) to (c) holds: a "when" definition, F45)

§ `ss 300 to 302 -- Offences`

-- The offence functions take the answers of ss 298(1) and 299 and of the defences (ss 303 to 316, aggregated below). A defence that applies is the text's no (fork F2).
-- src:5926 | 300 Every person who publishes a defamatory libel that they know is false is guilty of
-- src:5927 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:5928 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 300 (src:5926-5928)
GIVEN `the answer of s 298(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 299` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the defamatory libel is false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of ss 303 to 316` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 300 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel that they know is false` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of ss 303 to 316` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that"
        IF (`the answer of s 298(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 299` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person knows that the defamatory libel is false` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who publishes a defamatory libel that they know is false" (an element is missing or not determined)

@ref s 300 (src:5926-5928)
`s 300 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 300 (src:5927-5928)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 300 the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:5930 | 301 Every person who publishes a defamatory libel is guilty of
-- src:5931 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:5932 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 301 (src:5930-5932)
GIVEN `the answer of s 298(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 299` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of ss 303 to 316` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 301 the person is guilty of the offence of publishing a defamatory libel` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of ss 303 to 316` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that"
        IF (`the answer of s 298(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 299` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who publishes a defamatory libel" (an element is missing or not determined)

@ref s 301 (src:5930-5932)
`s 301 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 301 (src:5931-5932)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 301 the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:5934 | 302 (1) Every one commits an offence who, with intent
-- src:5935 | (a) to extort money from any person, or
-- src:5936 | (b) to induce a person to confer on or procure for another person an appointment or office of profit or trust,
-- src:5937 | publishes or threatens to publish or offers to abstain from publishing or to prevent the publication of a defamatory libel.
@ref s 302(1) (src:5934-5937)
GIVEN `the person acts with intent to extort money from any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts with intent to induce a person to confer on or procure for another person an appointment or office of profit or trust` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes or threatens to publish or offers to abstain from publishing or to prevent the publication of a defamatory libel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 302(1) the person commits the offence of extortion by libel` MEANS
    IF (`the person acts with intent to extort money from any person` OR `the person acts with intent to induce a person to confer on or procure for another person an appointment or office of profit or trust`) AND `the person publishes or threatens to publish or offers to abstain from publishing or to prevent the publication of a defamatory libel`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one commits an offence who, with intent (a) to extort money from any person, or (b) to induce a person to confer on or procure for another person an appointment or office of profit or trust, publishes or threatens to publish"

-- src:5938 | Idem
-- src:5939 | (2) Every one commits an offence who, as the result of the refusal of any person to permit money to be extorted or to confer or procure an appointment or office of profit or trust, publishes or threatens to publish a defamatory libel.
