`s 302(3) the person who commits an offence under this section is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF (`the answer of s 302(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of s 302(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who commits an offence under this section is guilty of"

@ref s 302(3) (src:5940-5943)
`s 302(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 302(3) (src:5941-5943)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 302(3) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `ss 303 and 304 -- Newspapers and sellers`

-- 303(1): a deeming rule with an "unless he proves": proved on both counts takes the deeming away (JUST FALSE). The newspaper is s 297's answer (taken as an input).
-- src:5944 | Proprietor of newspaper presumed responsible
-- src:5945 | 303 (1) The proprietor of a newspaper shall be deemed to publish defamatory matter that is inserted and published therein, unless he proves that the defamatory matter was inserted in the newspaper without his knowledge and without negligence on his part.
@ref s 303(1) (src:5944-5945)
GIVEN `the answer of s 297 as to the publication` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is the proprietor of the newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defamatory matter is inserted and published in the newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proprietor proves that the defamatory matter was inserted in the newspaper without his knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proprietor proves that it was inserted without negligence on his part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(1) the proprietor of a newspaper is deemed to publish the defamatory matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT ((`the answer of s 297 as to the publication` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the person is the proprietor of the newspaper` AND `the defamatory matter is inserted and published in the newspaper`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The proprietor of a newspaper shall be deemed to publish defamatory matter that is inserted and published therein" (a newspaper as s 297 has it)
        IF `the proprietor proves that the defamatory matter was inserted in the newspaper without his knowledge` AND `the proprietor proves that it was inserted without negligence on his part` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he proves that the defamatory matter was inserted in the newspaper without his knowledge and without negligence on his part"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:5946 | General authority to manager when negligence
-- src:5947 | (2) Where the proprietor of a newspaper gives to a person general authority to manage or conduct the newspaper as editor or otherwise, the insertion by that person of defamatory matter in the newspaper shall, for the purposes of subsection (1), be deemed not to be negligence on the part of the proprietor unless it is proved that
-- src:5948 | (a) he intended the general authority to include authority to insert defamatory matter in the newspaper; or
-- src:5949 | (b) he continued to confer general authority after he knew that it had been exercised by the insertion of defamatory matter in the newspaper.
@ref s 303(2) (src:5946-5949)
GIVEN `the proprietor of a newspaper gave a person general authority to manage or conduct the newspaper as editor or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person inserted defamatory matter in the newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the proprietor intended the general authority to include authority to insert defamatory matter in the newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the proprietor continued to confer general authority after he knew that it had been exercised by the insertion of defamatory matter in the newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(2) the insertion is deemed not to be negligence on the part of the proprietor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the proprietor of a newspaper gave a person general authority to manage or conduct the newspaper as editor or otherwise` AND `that person inserted defamatory matter in the newspaper`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the proprietor of a newspaper gives to a person general authority to manage or conduct the newspaper as editor or otherwise, the insertion by that person of defamatory matter in the newspaper"
        IF `it is proved that the proprietor intended the general authority to include authority to insert defamatory matter in the newspaper` OR `it is proved that the proprietor continued to confer general authority after he knew that it had been exercised by the insertion of defamatory matter in the newspaper` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is proved that (a) he intended the general authority to include authority to insert defamatory matter in the newspaper; or (b) he continued to confer general authority"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 303(3): "No person shall be deemed to publish ... by reason only that he sells a number or part of a newspaper ..., unless he knows".
-- src:5950 | Selling newspapers
-- src:5951 | (3) No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he sells a number or part of a newspaper that contains a defamatory libel, unless he knows that the number or part contains defamatory matter or that defamatory matter is habitually contained in the newspaper.
@ref s 303(3) (src:5950-5951)
GIVEN `the person’s only ground for saying he published is that he sells a number or part of a newspaper that contains a defamatory libel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he knows that the number or part contains defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he knows that defamatory matter is habitually contained in the newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 303(3) the seller of a number or part of a newspaper is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person’s only ground for saying he published is that he sells a number or part of a newspaper that contains a defamatory libel` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he sells a number or part of a newspaper that contains a defamatory libel"
        IF `he knows that the number or part contains defamatory matter` OR `he knows that defamatory matter is habitually contained in the newspaper` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he knows that the number or part contains defamatory matter or that defamatory matter is habitually contained in the newspaper"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:5953 | 304 (1) No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he sells a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing, other than a newspaper that contains defamatory matter, if, at the time of the sale, he does not know that it contains the defamatory matter.
@ref s 304(1) (src:5953)
GIVEN `the answer of s 297 as to the thing sold` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person’s only ground for saying he published is that he sells a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the sale he does not know that it contains the defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304(1) the seller of a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing is not deemed to publish the defamatory libel by reason only of the sale` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person’s only ground for saying he published is that he sells a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing` AND (`the answer of s 297 as to the thing sold` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he sells a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing, other than a newspaper that contains defamatory matter" (a newspaper is section 303(3)'s)
        IF `at the time of the sale he does not know that it contains the defamatory matter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, at the time of the sale, he does not know that it contains the defamatory matter" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:5954 | Sale by servant
-- src:5955 | (2) Where a servant, in the course of his employment, sells a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing, other than a newspaper, the employer shall be deemed not to publish any defamatory matter contained therein unless it is proved that the employer authorized the sale knowing that
-- src:5956 | (a) defamatory matter was contained therein; or
-- src:5957 | (b) defamatory matter was habitually contained therein, in the case of a periodical.
@ref s 304(2) (src:5954-5957)
GIVEN `the answer of s 297 as to the thing sold` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a servant, in the course of his employment, sells a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the employer authorized the sale knowing that defamatory matter was contained therein` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the employer authorized the sale knowing that defamatory matter was habitually contained therein, in the case of a periodical` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 304(2) the employer is deemed not to publish the defamatory matter contained in the thing sold` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a servant, in the course of his employment, sells a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing` AND (`the answer of s 297 as to the thing sold` EQUALS JUST FALSE)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a servant, in the course of his employment, sells a book, magazine, pamphlet or other thing, other than a newspaper"
        IF `it is proved that the employer authorized the sale knowing that defamatory matter was contained therein` OR `it is proved that the employer authorized the sale knowing that defamatory matter was habitually contained therein, in the case of a periodical` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is proved that the employer authorized the sale knowing that"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `ss 305 to 307 -- Proceedings of courts and of the legislatures`

-- src:5959 | 305 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes defamatory matter
-- src:5960 | (a) in a proceeding held before or under the authority of a court exercising judicial authority; or
-- src:5961 | (b) in an inquiry made under the authority of an Act or by order of Her Majesty, or under the authority of a public department or a department of the government of a province.
@ref s 305 (src:5959-5961)
GIVEN `the person publishes defamatory matter in a proceeding held before or under the authority of a court exercising judicial authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes defamatory matter in an inquiry made under the authority of an Act or by order of Her Majesty, or under the authority of a public department or a department of the government of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 305 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the matter in the proceeding or inquiry` MEANS
    IF `the person publishes defamatory matter in a proceeding held before or under the authority of a court exercising judicial authority` OR `the person publishes defamatory matter in an inquiry made under the authority of an Act or by order of Her Majesty, or under the authority of a public department or a department of the government of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he publishes defamatory matter (a) in a proceeding held before or under the authority of a court exercising judicial authority; or (b) in an inquiry made under the authority of an Act"

-- src:5963 | 306 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he
-- src:5964 | (a) publishes to the Senate or House of Commons or to the legislature of a province defamatory matter contained in a petition to the Senate or House of Commons or to the legislature of a province, as the case may be;
-- src:5965 | (b) publishes by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or of the legislature of a province a paper containing defamatory matter; or
-- src:5966 | (c) publishes, in good faith and without ill-will to the person defamed, an extract from or abstract of a petition or paper mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b).
@ref s 306 (src:5963-5966)
GIVEN `the person publishes to the Senate or House of Commons or to the legislature of a province defamatory matter contained in a petition to the Senate or House of Commons or to the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or of the legislature of a province a paper containing defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes an extract from or abstract of a petition or paper mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so in good faith and without ill-will to the person defamed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 306 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the petition or paper` MEANS
    IF `the person publishes to the Senate or House of Commons or to the legislature of a province defamatory matter contained in a petition to the Senate or House of Commons or to the legislature of a province`
       OR `the person publishes by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or of the legislature of a province a paper containing defamatory matter`
       OR (`the person publishes an extract from or abstract of a petition or paper mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` AND `the person does so in good faith and without ill-will to the person defamed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he (a) publishes to the Senate or House of Commons or to the legislature of a province defamatory matter contained in a petition", "(b) publishes by order or under the authority of the Senate", or "(c) publishes, in good faith and without ill-will to the person defamed, an extract"

-- src:5968 | 307 (1) No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes in good faith, for the information of the public, a fair report of the proceedings of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province, or a committee thereof, or of the public proceedings before a court exercising judicial authority, or publishes, in good faith, any fair comment on any such proceedings.
@ref s 307(1) (src:5968)
GIVEN `the person publishes in good faith, for the information of the public, a fair report of the proceedings of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province, or a committee thereof, or of the public proceedings before a court exercising judicial authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes, in good faith, any fair comment on any such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307(1) the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment` MEANS
    IF `the person publishes in good faith, for the information of the public, a fair report of the proceedings of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province, or a committee thereof, or of the public proceedings before a court exercising judicial authority` OR `the person publishes, in good faith, any fair comment on any such proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he publishes in good faith, for the information of the public, a fair report of the proceedings"

-- src:5969 | Divorce proceedings an exception
-- src:5970 | (2) This section does not apply to a person who publishes a report of evidence taken or offered in any proceeding before the Senate or House of Commons or any committee thereof, on a petition or bill relating to any matter of marriage or divorce, if the report is published without authority from or leave of the House in which the proceeding is held or is contrary to any rule, order or practice of that House.
@ref s 307(2) (src:5969-5970)
GIVEN `the person publishes a report of evidence taken or offered in any proceeding before the Senate or House of Commons or any committee thereof, on a petition or bill relating to any matter of marriage or divorce` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is published without authority from or leave of the House in which the proceeding is held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is published contrary to any rule, order or practice of that House` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307(2) section 307 does not apply to the person who publishes the report` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person publishes a report of evidence taken or offered in any proceeding before the Senate or House of Commons or any committee thereof, on a petition or bill relating to any matter of marriage or divorce` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not apply to a person who publishes a report of evidence taken or offered in any proceeding before the Senate or House of Commons or any committee thereof, on a petition or bill relating to any matter of marriage or divorce"
        IF `the report is published without authority from or leave of the House in which the proceeding is held` OR `the report is published contrary to any rule, order or practice of that House` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the report is published without authority from or leave of the House in which the proceeding is held or is contrary to any rule, order or practice of that House" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- Subsection (1) after the exception of (2): where (2) applies, section 307 does not apply and the immunity is JUST FALSE.
@ref s 307(1) composed with s 307(2) (src:5969-5970)
GIVEN `the answer of s 307(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 307(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report or fair comment, after subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 307(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to a person who publishes a report of evidence"
        IF (`the answer of s 307(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 307(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the immunity or the exception is not determined

§ `ss 308 to 315 -- Fair reports, public benefit, fair comment, truth, invitation, inquiries, information and redress`

-- 308: "by reason only that he publishes in good faith, in a newspaper, a fair report of the proceedings of any public meeting if (a) to (d)".
-- src:5972 | 308 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes in good faith, in a newspaper, a fair report of the proceedings of any public meeting if
-- src:5973 | (a) the meeting is lawfully convened for a lawful purpose and is open to the public;
-- src:5974 | (b) the report is fair and accurate;
-- src:5975 | (c) the publication of the matter complained of is for the public benefit; and
-- src:5976 | (d) he does not refuse to publish in a conspicuous place in the newspaper a reasonable explanation or contradiction by the person defamed in respect of the defamatory matter.
@ref s 308 (src:5972-5976)
GIVEN `the answer of s 297 as to the publication` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes in good faith, in a newspaper, a fair report of the proceedings of a public meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is lawfully convened for a lawful purpose and is open to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report is fair and accurate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the publication of the matter complained of is for the public benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not refuse to publish in a conspicuous place in the newspaper a reasonable explanation or contradiction by the person defamed in respect of the defamatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 308 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing the fair report of the public meeting` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person publishes in good faith, in a newspaper, a fair report of the proceedings of a public meeting` AND (`the answer of s 297 as to the publication` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he publishes in good faith, in a newspaper, a fair report of the proceedings of any public meeting"
        IF `the meeting is lawfully convened for a lawful purpose and is open to the public` AND `the report is fair and accurate` AND `the publication of the matter complained of is for the public benefit` AND `the person does not refuse to publish in a conspicuous place in the newspaper a reasonable explanation or contradiction by the person defamed in respect of the defamatory matter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) the meeting is lawfully convened for a lawful purpose and is open to the public; (b) the report is fair and accurate; (c) the publication of the matter complained of is for the public benefit; and (d) he does not refuse to publish" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:5978 | 309 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes defamatory matter that, on reasonable grounds, he believes is true, and that is relevant to any subject of public interest, the public discussion of which is for the public benefit.
@ref s 309 (src:5978)
GIVEN `the person publishes defamatory matter that, on reasonable grounds, he believes is true` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is relevant to a subject of public interest, the public discussion of which is for the public benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 309 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing matter believed true that is relevant to a subject of public interest` MEANS
    IF `the person publishes defamatory matter that, on reasonable grounds, he believes is true` AND `the matter is relevant to a subject of public interest, the public discussion of which is for the public benefit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he publishes defamatory matter that, on reasonable grounds, he believes is true, and that is relevant to any subject of public interest, the public discussion of which is for the public benefit"

-- src:5980 | 310 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes fair comments
-- src:5981 | (a) on the public conduct of a person who takes part in public affairs; or
-- src:5982 | (b) on a published book or other literary production, or on any composition or work of art or performance publicly exhibited, or on any other communication made to the public on any subject, if the comments are confined to criticism thereof.
@ref s 310 (src:5980-5982)
GIVEN `the person publishes fair comments on the public conduct of a person who takes part in public affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes fair comments on a published book or other literary production, or on any composition or work of art or performance publicly exhibited, or on any other communication made to the public on any subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the comments are confined to criticism thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 310 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing fair comments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person publishes fair comments on the public conduct of a person who takes part in public affairs` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person publishes fair comments on a published book or other literary production, or on any composition or work of art or performance publicly exhibited, or on any other communication made to the public on any subject` AND `the comments are confined to criticism thereof` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person publishes fair comments on a published book or other literary production, or on any composition or work of art or performance publicly exhibited, or on any other communication made to the public on any subject` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the comments are confined to criticism thereof" (the comments are not confined to criticism: this section gives no defence on these facts)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he publishes fair comments (a) on the public conduct of a person who takes part in public affairs; or (b) on a published book or other literary production"

-- 311: where he proves both limbs; not proved is "no defence on these facts".
-- src:5984 | 311 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel where he proves that the publication of the defamatory matter in the manner in which it was published was for the public benefit at the time when it was published and that the matter itself was true.
@ref s 311 (src:5984)
GIVEN `the person proves that the publication of the defamatory matter in the manner in which it was published was for the public benefit at the time when it was published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that the matter itself was true` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel where the person proves the publication was for the public benefit and the matter was true` MEANS
    IF `the person proves that the publication of the defamatory matter in the manner in which it was published was for the public benefit at the time when it was published` AND `the person proves that the matter itself was true`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where he proves that the publication of the defamatory matter in the manner in which it was published was for the public benefit at the time when it was published and that the matter itself was true" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:5986 | 312 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes defamatory matter
-- src:5987 | (a) on the invitation or challenge of the person in respect of whom it is published, or
-- src:5988 | (b) that it is necessary to publish in order to refute defamatory matter published in respect of him by another person,
-- src:5989 | if he believes that the defamatory matter is true and it is relevant to the invitation, challenge or necessary refutation, as the case may be, and does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances.
@ref s 312 (src:5986-5989)
GIVEN `the person publishes defamatory matter on the invitation or challenge of the person in respect of whom it is published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes defamatory matter that it is necessary to publish in order to refute defamatory matter published in respect of him by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he believes that the defamatory matter is true` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is relevant to the invitation, challenge or necessary refutation, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 312 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing on invitation or challenge, or to refute` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person publishes defamatory matter on the invitation or challenge of the person in respect of whom it is published` OR `the person publishes defamatory matter that it is necessary to publish in order to refute defamatory matter published in respect of him by another person`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he publishes defamatory matter (a) on the invitation or challenge of the person in respect of whom it is published, or (b) that it is necessary to publish in order to refute defamatory matter"
        IF `he believes that the defamatory matter is true` AND `it is relevant to the invitation, challenge or necessary refutation, as the case may be` AND `it does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if he believes that the defamatory matter is true and it is relevant to the invitation, challenge or necessary refutation, as the case may be, and does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:5991 | 313 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes, in answer to inquiries made to him, defamatory matter relating to a subject-matter in respect of which the person by whom or on whose behalf the inquiries are made has an interest in knowing the truth or who, on reasonable grounds, the person who publishes the defamatory matter believes has such an interest, if
-- src:5992 | (a) the matter is published, in good faith, for the purpose of giving information in answer to the inquiries;
-- src:5993 | (b) the person who publishes the defamatory matter believes that it is true;
-- src:5994 | (c) the defamatory matter is relevant to the inquiries; and
-- src:5995 | (d) the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances.
@ref s 313 (src:5991-5995)
GIVEN `the person publishes, in answer to inquiries made to him, defamatory matter relating to a subject-matter in which the inquirer has an interest in knowing the truth or, on reasonable grounds, is believed to have such an interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is published, in good faith, for the purpose of giving information in answer to the inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who publishes the defamatory matter believes that it is true` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defamatory matter is relevant to the inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 313 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in answer to inquiries` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person publishes, in answer to inquiries made to him, defamatory matter relating to a subject-matter in which the inquirer has an interest in knowing the truth or, on reasonable grounds, is believed to have such an interest` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he publishes, in answer to inquiries made to him, defamatory matter relating to a subject-matter in respect of which the person by whom or on whose behalf the inquiries are made has an interest in knowing the truth"
        IF `the matter is published, in good faith, for the purpose of giving information in answer to the inquiries` AND `the person who publishes the defamatory matter believes that it is true` AND `the defamatory matter is relevant to the inquiries` AND `the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) the matter is published, in good faith, for the purpose of giving information in answer to the inquiries; (b) the person who publishes the defamatory matter believes that it is true; (c) the defamatory matter is relevant to the inquiries; and (d) the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:5997 | 314 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes to another person defamatory matter for the purpose of giving information to that person with respect to a subject-matter in which the person to whom the information is given has, or is believed on reasonable grounds by the person who gives it to have, an interest in knowing the truth with respect to that subject-matter if
-- src:5998 | (a) the conduct of the person who gives the information is reasonable in the circumstances;
-- src:5999 | (b) the defamatory matter is relevant to the subject-matter; and
-- src:6000 | (c) the defamatory matter is true, or if it is not true, is made without ill-will toward the person who is defamed and is made in the belief, on reasonable grounds, that it is true.
@ref s 314 (src:5997-6000)
GIVEN `the person publishes to another person defamatory matter for the purpose of giving information to that person with respect to a subject-matter in which that person has, or is believed on reasonable grounds to have, an interest in knowing the truth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct of the person who gives the information is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defamatory matter is relevant to the subject-matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defamatory matter is true` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if it is not true, it is made without ill-will toward the person who is defamed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `if it is not true, it is made in the belief, on reasonable grounds, that it is true` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 314 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of giving information to a person interested` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person publishes to another person defamatory matter for the purpose of giving information to that person with respect to a subject-matter in which that person has, or is believed on reasonable grounds to have, an interest in knowing the truth` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he publishes to another person defamatory matter for the purpose of giving information to that person with respect to a subject-matter in which the person to whom the information is given has, or is believed on reasonable grounds by the person who gives it to have, an interest in knowing the truth"
        IF `the conduct of the person who gives the information is reasonable in the circumstances` AND `the defamatory matter is relevant to the subject-matter` AND (`the defamatory matter is true` OR (`if it is not true, it is made without ill-will toward the person who is defamed` AND `if it is not true, it is made in the belief, on reasonable grounds, that it is true`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) the conduct of the person who gives the information is reasonable in the circumstances; (b) the defamatory matter is relevant to the subject-matter; and (c) the defamatory matter is true, or if it is not true, is made without ill-will toward the person who is defamed" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

-- src:6002 | 315 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes defamatory matter in good faith for the purpose of seeking remedy or redress for a private or public wrong or grievance from a person who has, or who on reasonable grounds he believes has, the right or is under an obligation to remedy or redress the wrong or grievance, if
-- src:6003 | (a) he believes that the defamatory matter is true;
-- src:6004 | (b) the defamatory matter is relevant to the remedy or redress that is sought; and
-- src:6005 | (c) the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances.
@ref s 315 (src:6002-6005)
GIVEN `the person publishes defamatory matter in good faith for the purpose of seeking remedy or redress for a private or public wrong or grievance from a person who has, or who on reasonable grounds he believes has, the right or is under an obligation to remedy or redress the wrong or grievance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he believes that the defamatory matter is true` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defamatory matter is relevant to the remedy or redress that is sought` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 315 the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only of publishing in good faith to seek redress of a wrong` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person publishes defamatory matter in good faith for the purpose of seeking remedy or redress for a private or public wrong or grievance from a person who has, or who on reasonable grounds he believes has, the right or is under an obligation to remedy or redress the wrong or grievance` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that he publishes defamatory matter in good faith for the purpose of seeking remedy or redress for a private or public wrong or grievance"
        IF `he believes that the defamatory matter is true` AND `the defamatory matter is relevant to the remedy or redress that is sought` AND `the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) he believes that the defamatory matter is true; (b) the defamatory matter is relevant to the remedy or redress that is sought; and (c) the defamatory matter does not in any respect exceed what is reasonably sufficient in the circumstances" (this section gives no defence on these facts)

§ `s 316 -- Proving publication by order of the legislature`

-- 316(1): "may ... adduce evidence" is a grant: a missing element gives NOTHING (fork F4).
-- src:6007 | 316 (1) An accused who is alleged to have published a defamatory libel may, at any stage of the proceedings, adduce evidence to prove that the matter that is alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province.
@ref s 316(1) (src:6007)
GIVEN `the accused is alleged to have published a defamatory libel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is to prove that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 316(1) the accused may, at any stage of the proceedings, adduce evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` MEANS
    IF `the accused is alleged to have published a defamatory libel` AND `the evidence is to prove that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An accused who is alleged to have published a defamatory libel may, at any stage of the proceedings, adduce evidence to prove that the matter that is alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province"

-- src:6009 | (2) Where at any stage in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge is satisfied that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province, he shall direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and shall discharge the accused.
@ref s 316(2) (src:6009)
GIVEN `at some stage in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge is satisfied that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 316(2) the court shall direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and shall discharge the accused` MEANS
    IF `at some stage in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge is satisfied that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where at any stage in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge is satisfied that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province" (a failed "Where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

DECLARE `s 316(2) the act of the court` IS ONE OF `s 316(2) direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and discharge the accused`

@ref s 316(2) (src:6009)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 316(2) the act of the court`
`s 316(2) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 316(2) direct a verdict of not guilty to be entered and discharge the accused`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "no verdict of not guilty was directed although the court was satisfied that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature"

-- src:6011 | (3) For the purposes of this section, a certificate under the hand of the Speaker or clerk of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province to the effect that the matter that is alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate, House of Commons or the legislature of a province, as the case may be, is conclusive evidence thereof.
@ref s 316(3) (src:6011)
GIVEN `the certificate is under the hand of the Speaker or clerk of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to the effect that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate, House of Commons or the legislature of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 316(3) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the matter was contained in a paper published by order of the legislature` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is under the hand of the Speaker or clerk of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province` AND `it is to the effect that the matter alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper published by order or under the authority of the Senate, House of Commons or the legislature of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate under the hand of the Speaker or clerk of the Senate or House of Commons or the legislature of a province to the effect that the matter that is alleged to be defamatory was contained in a paper"

-- The cases in which a person is not deemed to publish, taken together: any one that applies shields the person. Defences that answer NOTHING do not speak to the facts (fork F44).
-- src:5959 | 305 No person shall be deemed to publish a defamatory libel by reason only that he publishes defamatory matter
@ref ss 303 to 316 (the form of each: s 305's lead-in) (src:5959)
GIVEN `the answers of the provisions that say a person is not deemed to publish` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 303 to 316 a provision says the person is not deemed to publish a defamatory libel` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN YIELD a EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the answers of the provisions that say a person is not deemed to publish`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no listed provision shields the person on these facts; the text does not say that no other lawful justification or excuse exists (s 298(1))

§ `s 317 -- Verdicts in cases of defamatory libel`

-- 317: one gate ("Where, on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded"); four limbs. "may" functions with a "Where" gate answer JUST FALSE
-- outside the gate under ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 and are listed in the fork register (F46) for a lawyer.
-- src:6015 | 317 Where, on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded, the jury that is sworn to try the issue may give a general verdict of guilty or not guilty on the whole matter put in issue on the indictment, and shall not be required or directed by the judge to find the defendant guilty merely on proof of publication by the defendant of the alleged defamatory libel, and of the sense ascribed thereto in the indictment, but the judge may, in his discretion, give a direction or opinion to the jury on the matter in issue as in other criminal proceedings, and the jury may, on the issue, find a special verdict.
@ref s 317 (src:6015)
GIVEN `on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jury is sworn to try the issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 317 the jury may give a general verdict of guilty or not guilty on the whole matter put in issue on the indictment` MEANS
    IF `on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded` AND `the jury is sworn to try the issue`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded, the jury that is sworn to try the issue may give a general verdict" (a failed "Where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); F46)

@ref s 317 (src:6015)
GIVEN `on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jury is sworn to try the issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 317 the jury shall not be required or directed by the judge to find the defendant guilty merely on proof of publication and of the sense ascribed` MEANS
    IF `on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded` AND `the jury is sworn to try the issue`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded" (a failed "Where": the bar is stated only inside its gate)

@ref s 317 (src:6015)
GIVEN `on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 317 the judge may, in his discretion, give a direction or opinion to the jury on the matter in issue as in other criminal proceedings` MEANS
    IF `on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, on the trial of an indictment for publishing a defamatory libel, a plea of not guilty is pleaded" (a failed "Where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); F46)

